{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788971444,"nonce":"+r8d8BKPyLucZQMDRHXu8U0XYbw=","message":"SCOPING PASS, 2026-09-09. Read-only against decompiled 1.6 and shipped Biotech/Core defs. No bench was touched.\n\nThe premise holds — nothing in the 139 verbs can summon a bossgroup — and the instinct to scope it with `d318d4a` is exactly right. But the route is a different shape than the body describes, the cost analysis is about the wrong boss, one acceptance bullet is unsatisfiable, and the open question is already answered by an existing issue.\n\n=====================================================================\nCORRECTIONS\n=====================================================================\n\n**1. `MechbandDish` is Apocriton's caller ONLY, and the ladder's first rung is a plain comms console.**\nThe link is inverted from what the body assumes: `BossgroupDef` has **no** `bossgroupCaller`/`callerThing` field. The *ThingDef* names the bossgroup via `CompProperties_Useable_CallBossgroup.bossgroupDef`, and `CallBossgroupUtility.GetBossgroupCaller(def)` reverse-scans the DefDatabase for it. Shipped, from `Biotech/Defs/BossgroupDefs/Bossgroups.xml` plus the three caller defs:\n\n| Bossgroup | Caller ThingDef | Caller research | Single-use? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Diabolus | **`CommsConsole`** (Core, `MayRequire` Biotech) | `MicroelectronicsBasics` (3000) | **no** — the console survives |\n| Warqueen | **`BurnoutMechlinkBooster`** (\"mechband antenna\") | `StandardMechtech` (1000) | yes |\n| Apocriton | `MechbandDish` | `HighMechtech` (3000) | yes |\n\nSo the whole \"What it costs to get there\" section is about the LAST rung. **Diabolus is summonable from the comms console every colony already builds**, and the real progression lock is not research cost — it is `requiredAnalyzed`: `HighMechtech` needs a `PowerfocusChip`, which only drops from a dead Warqueen, which needs `StandardMechtech`, which needs a `SignalChip` off a dead Diabolus. You must beat boss N to research the caller for boss N+1.\n\n**2. The research numbers are all correct (7/7), but the chain as drawn has a dependency that does not exist.** `MicroelectronicsBasics`' prerequisite is `Electricity`, not `StandardMechtech` — the two are parallel branches, not a spine. And `HighMechtech` has **two** prerequisites (`StandardMechtech` AND `MultiAnalyzer`), plus `requiredResearchBuilding HiTechResearchBench` and `requiredResearchFacilities MultiAnalyzer`.\n\n**3. `appearAfterTicks` is on `BossDef`, not `BossgroupDef`, and it is not a summon gate at all.**\n`BossDef.appearAfterTicks` (`int.MaxValue` default; Diabolus 7,200,000 / Warqueen 14,400,000 / Apocriton 21,600,000). Its only two consumers are `GameComponent_Bossgroup.ReservedByBossgroup` — which stops that mech kind appearing in ordinary raids and mech clusters until the time passes — and a debug table. **A player can summon Diabolus on day 1** given a powered comms console and a mechanitor. \"the dish is how a player picks the fight earlier\" is right in spirit; the number is not a gate on this verb and citing it as one will send a worker looking for a check that isn't there.\n\n**4. There is no `IsDisabled(out string reason)` you can call, and `gizmo.Disabled` is unreadable headless.**\n`Command_CallBossgroup` has no `Disabled` override and no `GizmoDisabled`. It has a **private** `IsDisabled(out string reason)` invoked from a `GizmoOnGUI` override that writes the base `Gizmo.disabled` / `Gizmo.disabledReason` fields **every paint frame**. On a bench where nothing paints, those fields hold their defaults or whatever the last paint left. A verb must call the underlying predicates directly.\n\n**5. The gizmo chain is FIVE checks, not three.** Verbatim order from `IsDisabled`:\n  1. `Faction.OfMechanoids == null || .deactivated` → `\"MechsDisabled\"`\n  2. `!mechanitor.Pawn.health.capacities.CapableOf(PawnCapacityDefOf.Manipulation)` → `\"Incapable\"` (a **Core** key)\n  3. `TicksGame - Find.BossgroupManager.lastBossgroupCalled \u003c 120000` → `\"BossgroupAvailableIn\"` with the remainder as a period\n  4. **[MISSING FROM THE BODY]** `CallBossgroupUtility.GetPendingBossgroup() != null` → `\"BossgroupIncoming\"` — scans `Find.QuestManager` for an Ongoing quest with a `QuestPart_Bossgroup` whose bosses are all unspawned and alive, i.e. \"one is already inbound\"\n  5. **[MISSING]** `FloatMenuOptions.All(f =\u003e f.action == null)` → disabled with **`reason = null`**, a silent disable. This is `BossgroupEverCallable` folded across every `BossgroupDef`.\n\n**6. `BossgroupEverCallable` is FIVE refusals, not four, and the power one is conditional.**\n  0. `if (!pawn.Spawned) return false;` — **bare `false`, no reason string**. This is the missing first clause.\n  1. `list.Count \u003c= 0` → `\"NoSubject\"` (a **Core** key: `No {0}`)\n  2. nothing `CanReach(…, PathEndMode.InteractionCell, Danger.Deadly)` → `\"NoReachableBossgroupCaller\"`\n  3. nothing `CanReserve(…, forced)` → `\"NoReservableBossgroupCaller\"`\n  4. **only when** `bossgroupCaller.HasComp(typeof(CompPowerTrader))** — no instance `PowerOn` → `\"NoPoweredBossgroupCaller\"`. `MechbandDish` and `BurnoutMechlinkBooster` have **no** `CompProperties_Power`, so this refusal is unreachable for two of the three bossgroups. Only Diabolus/CommsConsole can produce it.\n\n  And it checks **none** of the cooldown, `appearAfterTicks`, mechanitor-ness or manipulation. Those live elsewhere (see addition A).\n\n**7. `PathEndMode` asymmetry, and the two can disagree.** `BossgroupEverCallable` tests `PathEndMode.InteractionCell`; `TryStartSummonBossgroupJob` tests `PathEndMode.Touch`. `CommsConsole` has `hasInteractionCell true` and the other two do not. So a caller can be `callable:true` and then not selected by the dispatcher, or vice versa. Report which mode produced which verdict.\n\n**8. `Find.BossgroupManager` is not a `BossgroupManager`.** `Verse/Find.cs`: `public static GameComponent_Bossgroup BossgroupManager =\u003e Current.Game.GetComponent\u003cGameComponent_Bossgroup\u003e();` — **it can return null**, and `CompUseEffect_CallBossgroup.CallBossgroup` guards it with a `Log.Error`. There is no `BossgroupManager` type. State is `public int lastBossgroupCalled = -9999999;` plus a private `Dictionary\u003cBossgroupDef,int\u003e timesCalledBossgroups`; the accessor is `NumTimesCalledBossgroup(BossgroupDef)`, not `NumTimesCalled`. The named constant for the cooldown is `BossgroupWorker.TimeBetweenAllBossgroups = 120000`; `IsDisabled` uses the bare literal twice and does not reference it.\n\n**9. `repeatWaveStartIndex: 2` is right but \"escalate per call\" is not what happens after wave 7.**\nAll three bossgroups ship 8 waves and inherit `repeatWaveStartIndex 2` from the abstract `BaseBossgroup`. `BossgroupDef.GetWaveIndex(timesSummoned)` is linear for the first 8, then:\n```\nRand.PushState(Gen.HashCombine(Find.World.info.Seed, timesSummoned));\nnum = Rand.Range(repeatWaveStartIndex, waves.Count);\nRand.PopState();\n```\n— a world-seed-deterministic **random pick in [2,8)**, not a monotonic escalation. (The `PushState`/`PopState` pair means it does not burn the shared stream, so this is safe to evaluate from a read verb — worth knowing, since `WorldSafe` Class R would otherwise disqualify it.) Diabolus wave 3 content is exactly right; it also carries `bossApparel: Apparel_HeavyShield`, worn `locked:true`, on both bosses.\n\n**10. The mechanitor test to cite is `MechanitorUtility.IsMechanitor(pawn)`, not `Pawn.mechanitor`.** `Pawn.mechanitor` is a real public field (`Pawn_MechanitorTracker`), but the predicate is `ModsConfig.BiotechActive \u0026\u0026 pawn.Faction.IsPlayerSafe() \u0026\u0026 hediffSet.HasHediff(HediffDefOf.MechlinkImplant)` **and then** `pawn.mechanitor != null`. Naming the field alone would produce a refusal that says the wrong thing for a mechlinked pawn who changed faction.\n\n**11. \"Waves escalate per call … so this is a repeatable ladder\" — only for Diabolus without rebuilding.** `MechbandDish` and `BurnoutMechlinkBooster` both carry `CompProperties_UseEffectDestroySelf` (120 ticks, `spawnKilledLeavings`), so they are consumed by the summon. `CommsConsole` has no such comp.\n\n=====================================================================\nADDITIONS\n=====================================================================\n\n**A. THERE IS A THIRD GATE CHAIN, IT IS THE AUTHORITATIVE ONE, AND IT DISAGREES WITH THE GIZMO.**\n`CompUseEffect_CallBossgroup.CanBeUsedBy(Pawn p)`:\n```\nif (Faction.OfMechanoids == null || Faction.OfMechanoids.deactivated) return \"MechsDisabled\".Translate();\nif (!MechanitorUtility.IsMechanitor(p)) return \"RequiresMechanitor\".Translate();\nreturn Props.bossgroupDef.Worker.CanResolve(p);\n```\nand `BossgroupWorker.CanResolve` re-checks the 120,000-tick cooldown (`\"BossgroupAvailableIn\"`) and `GetPendingBossgroup` (`\"BossgroupIncoming\"`).\nBecause this is a `CompUseEffect`, `CompUsable.CanBeUsedBy` runs it as its last clause — so it is enforced at the float menu, again inside `TryStartUseJob`, again continuously by `JobDriver_UseItem`'s `FailOn`, and again in `UsedBy`. **The gizmo's `IsDisabled` is a duplicate of it plus Manipulation minus the caller checks.**\nThe disagreement matters: `Command_CallBossgroup.IsDisabled` refuses a manipulation-incapable mechanitor; `CompUsable.CanBeUsedBy` does not, and neither does the float-menu provider (`RequiresManipulation =\u003e false`). Manipulation is only `JobDriver_UseItem`'s `FailOnIncapable`. **So the two player routes have different preconditions, and a verb that reproduces \"the gizmo's chain\" will refuse something a player can do by right-clicking the console** — the `261f2e9` error facing the other way. Reproduce the `CanBeUsedBy` chain as the gate; report Manipulation as an advisory citing the job driver.\n\n**B. THE ACT IS `use`. This issue does not need a new act verb.**\n`CompUsable.CompFloatMenuOptions` yields the option on the caller building itself (`useLabel` = \"Summon apocriton threat\" / the console's equivalent) for any colonist right-clicking it. `CallBossgroupUtility.TryStartSummonBossgroupJob` is nothing but a picker in front of it:\n```\nList\u003cThing\u003e list = pawn.Map.listerThings.ThingsOfDef(GetBossgroupCaller(def));\nlist.SortBy(t =\u003e t.Position.DistanceToSquared(pawn.Position));\nfor (…) if (pawn.CanReserveAndReach(list[num], PathEndMode.Touch, Danger.Deadly, 1, -1, null, forced)\n            \u0026\u0026 (bool)list[num].TryGetComp\u003cCompUsable\u003e().CanBeUsedBy(pawn))\n        { list[num].TryGetComp\u003cCompUsable\u003e().TryStartUseJob(pawn, null, forced); break; }\n```\n`forced` defaults to **`true`** here and in `BossgroupEverCallable` — unusual, and it changes the reservation test. Note it also `SortBy`s the **live `listerThings` list in place**; a verb reproducing this must snapshot first.\n\n**C. THE ACCEPTANCE BULLET \"routes through `CallBossgroupUtility.TryStartSummonBossgroupJob` — never by constructing the quest directly\" IS UNSATISFIABLE AS WRITTEN.**\n`CompUseEffect_CallBossgroup.ConfirmMessage(p)` is **always non-empty** — `\"BossgroupWarningDialog\".Translate(leaderkind, GetWaveDescription(…))`. So `TryStartUseJob` always takes the branch\n`Find.WindowStack.Add(Dialog_MessageBox.CreateConfirmation(text, StartJob))`, and `Dialog_MessageBox : Window` with `forcePause = true`. Per spec 1.7 every subsequent `advance` halts at 0 ticks; and no shipped verb can press Accept — `dialog-choose` takes a `Dialog_NodeTree`, `dialog-accept` takes a text-entry naming window, and `dialog-dismiss` would **cancel** the summon. **Calling `TryStartSummonBossgroupJob` from a verb wedges the run and does not summon anything.**\nReplacement bullet: routes through `d318d4a`'s reproduced `StartJob`, and publishes `BossgroupDef.GetWaveDescription(waveIndex)` — the exact text of the confirmation — as the disclosed `dialogs_skipped` field, the shipped `equip`/`wear` pattern. The agent should be told what it is about to fight; that is the whole content of the modal.\n\n**D. `NumTimesCalledBossgroup` INSERTS INTO A SCRIBED DICTIONARY ON A MISS — a read verb must not call it.**\n```\npublic int NumTimesCalledBossgroup(BossgroupDef d)\n{ if (!timesCalledBossgroups.ContainsKey(d)) timesCalledBossgroups.Add(d, 0); return timesCalledBossgroups[d]; }\n```\nand `ExposeData` does `Scribe_Collections.Look(ref timesCalledBossgroups, \"timesCalledBossgroups\", LookMode.Def, LookMode.Value, …)`. **This is `WorldSafe` Class A exactly** — the `ResearchManager.GetProgress` shape that `WorldSafe.CanStart`/`Finished` exist to route around. Asking \"how many times have I called each bossgroup?\" would add three entries to the save, permanently. The `bossgroups` read must reach the private dictionary with `TryGetValue` through an `AccessTools.FieldRef` and default 0, and say so at the call site. The act path may call the public getter (the player's click does).\n\n**E. `Notify_BossgroupCalled`'s else-branch adds 0, not 1.** It is benign only because `NumTimesCalledBossgroup(def)` is always evaluated first as an argument and pre-creates the key. A verb must never call `Notify_BossgroupCalled` itself — `BossgroupWorker.Resolve` does it, and doing it twice would double the cooldown stamp and lose an increment.\n\n**F. `GetBossgroupCaller` memoises `cachedBossCallers` on first call and never invalidates it.** That is a `PawnSafe` Class F memo (not scribed, recomputed from defs) and is fine — the same disposition as Nepo's `CatalogBuilder` list builders. Named so it is a decision, not an oversight.\n\n**G. The success shape is a QuestScriptDef, and the letters do not arrive together.**\n`BossgroupWorker.Resolve(map, wave)` → `Find.BossgroupManager.Notify_BossgroupCalled(def)` → `QuestUtility.GenerateQuestAndMakeAvailable(def.quest, slate)` where `def.quest` is `QuestScriptDef Bossgroup` (`defaultHidden true`, `autoAccept true`, root `QuestNode_Root_Bossgroup`). No `IncidentDef` anywhere.\n  * **Immediately**: a `LetterDefOf.NeutralEvent` `\"LetterLabelBossgroupSummoned\"`, and the critical `AlertBossgroupIncoming`.\n  * **Later**: `QuestPart_BossgroupArrives` with `minDelay = IntRange(2500,5000).RandomInRange` and `maxDelay = IntRange(60000,180000).RandomInRange`, polling `BossgroupWorker.ShouldSummonNow(map)` every 2500 ticks (it returns false during a trade/bestowing/visit lord job). Then the drop pods and a `LetterDefOf.Bossgroup` `\"LetterLabelBossgroupArrived\"`.\n  Split the acceptance bullet accordingly: summoned-letter + alert are same-advance; the `Bossgroup` letter is **2,500–180,000 ticks** later and must not be asserted in the same window.\n\n**H. `lastBossgroupCalled` advances at `DoEffect`, not at order time** — after the caller's `useDuration` (900 ticks on the dish) elapses. The cooldown acceptance therefore needs an `advance` past the job before the second call is attempted, or it will test the wrong thing.\n\n**I. `ModsConfig.BiotechActive` is the outermost gate.** `CompUseEffect_CallBossgroup.PostSpawnSetup` runs `ModLister.CheckBiotech(\"Call bossgroup\")` and **destroys the parent** if Biotech is off. The verb needs a Biotech-absent refusal ahead of everything, in the same spirit as `nepo-absent`.\n\n**J. `Command_CallBossgroup.DescPostfix` is the model for the read.** It already builds a per-def `Dictionary\u003cBossgroupDef, AcceptanceReport\u003e` from `BossgroupEverCallable` for the tooltip. Do not call it (it is a UI member that formats colour tags); call `BossgroupEverCallable` per def directly, which is what it does.\n\n=====================================================================\nOPEN QUESTION SETTLED: specific, not generic — and the specific one is smaller than the issue thinks\n=====================================================================\n**The generic `gizmo-activate` is already filed as git-bug `9717e52`** (\"No verb reads or presses a thing's GIZMOS\", open, p1, `wave:6`), whose comment #1 records Dorian's own objection that a press-only verb is useless because the interesting gizmos open multi-step flows. Filing a second generic verb here would fork it. That alone settles the question, but four independent reasons say the generic verb could not satisfy the action model anyway:\n\n1. **`Command.ProcessInput` performs NO disabled check.** Its entire body is `if (CurActivateSound != null) CurActivateSound.PlayOneShotOnCamera();`, and `Command_Action.ProcessInput` is `base.ProcessInput(ev); action();`. The disabled test lives in `Command.GizmoOnGUI`, which needs a `Rect` and `Event.current` and, when `disabled`, shows a message and returns `GizmoResult(GizmoState.Mouseover, null)` without ever reaching `ProcessInput`. A generic presser therefore bypasses **every** `disabledReason` in the game — a god-hand, which DESIGN §Action model forbids for a player verb.\n2. **A gizmo cannot supply a `gate`.** `Outcome.No(pawn, gate, reason)` wants a machine-readable clause name plus the game's own string. A `Command` offers only `disabledReason`, a translated sentence — and `Command_CallBossgroup`'s fifth branch sets it to **`null`**. `by_gate` aggregation would be a histogram of one bucket.\n3. **For this gizmo the disabled state does not exist outside a paint frame** (correction 4). Reading `gizmo.Disabled` headless is reading stale UI state.\n4. **Enumerating the gizmo list is itself an observer hazard.** `Pawn.GetGizmos()` branches on `Find.Selector.SingleSelectedThing == this` and `Find.Selector.SelectedPawns.Count \u003c 2`, so the set depends on UI selection and is wrong on an unattended bench; and one branch evaluates `DevelopmentalStage.Child()` — `PawnSafe` Class C, which routes through `Pawn_AgeTracker.CurLifeStageIndex` and can rename the pawn and add/remove components.\n\n**But the specific verb should be smaller than this issue assumes, because the act belongs to `d318d4a`.** What ships here:\n  * **`bossgroups` — the read, and it is the real deliverable.** Per `BossgroupDef`: boss kind, `GetBossgroupCaller` def, whether any instance exists / is reachable (`InteractionCell`) / is reservable / is powered-if-it-has-power, the global cooldown remaining, whether one is already pending, the current wave index (via the guarded route in addition D) and `GetWaveDescription` of what would arrive, and a `callable` verdict with the game's own reason. No analogue exists in the tree.\n  * **`bossgroup-call {pawn, bossgroup}` as a PICKER over `use`, not a second gate chain.** It resolves `BossgroupDef → GetBossgroupCaller → nearest reachable+reservable instance` on a snapshot, then calls `d318d4a`'s internal use path with `forced: true`. Worth shipping — the picker is real work and `use {pawn, thing:\u003cthe right console\u003e}` requires the agent to already know which building is which boss's caller — but it is ~40 lines on top of `use`, and it must not re-implement `CanBeUsedBy`.\n  * The acceptance's \"The pawn argument must be a mechanitor\" is then automatic: `CompUseEffect_CallBossgroup.CanBeUsedBy` produces `\"RequiresMechanitor\"` inside the shared chain. Cite `MechanitorUtility.IsMechanitor`.\n\n=====================================================================\nSIZE AND DEPENDENCY\n=====================================================================\n**Hard dependency on `d318d4a`.** Without `use`'s reproduced `StartJob`, the only route is `TryStartSummonBossgroupJob`, which wedges the run (addition C). Dispatch after it; do not dispatch in parallel.\n\n**Size: one file, ~250–350 lines.** `bossgroups` ~180 (three-per-def gate evaluation, the `AccessTools.FieldRef` around `timesCalledBossgroups`, wave description, the Biotech gate); `bossgroup-call` ~60 as a picker; ~40 of header citing the three chains and their disagreements.\n\n**The risky part is the scribed-dictionary insert (D).** A `bossgroups` read that calls the public `NumTimesCalledBossgroup` looks completely correct, returns the right number, and writes three permanent entries into the save every time the agent asks what it could summon. It is the `ResearchManager.GetProgress` trap in a new place, and the only thing standing between a worker and it is a comment.\n\n**Second risk: whose chain to reproduce.** Three overlapping gate sets exist (gizmo, `BossgroupEverCallable`, `CompUseEffect_CallBossgroup` + `BossgroupWorker.CanResolve`) and they disagree on Manipulation and on `PathEndMode`. Reproducing the gizmo's, which is what the issue body describes, fabricates a restriction the float-menu route does not have.\n\n**Priority note:** `p2` looks right and possibly generous. The dish needs a dead Warqueen upstream of it, and the whole ladder needs a mechanitor — which needs `Mechlink`, which is unusable until `d318d4a` ships. The `bossgroups` READ is worth having early regardless, because it is the only thing that would tell an agent the ladder exists.","files":null}]}